1
00:00:01,580 --> 00:00:04,857
Before we get things started,
there's something I want to check.

2
00:00:04,940 --> 00:00:07,705
How about you go ahead
and shuffle those cards?

3
00:00:20,200 --> 00:00:21,760
And, shuffled they are.

4
00:00:22,180 --> 00:00:24,560
What pray tell do you have in mind next?

5
00:00:25,100 --> 00:00:26,940
Now draw a card from the deck.

6
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:30,877
Which one it is doesn't really
make a whole lot of difference.

7
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:32,720
But don't show anyone.

8
00:00:35,460 --> 00:00:36,290
Very well.

9
00:00:36,980 --> 00:00:38,420
And now I'll call it.

10
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:39,953
It's the Six of Hearts.

11
00:00:40,580 --> 00:00:43,137
Next, I think I'll name the
cards from the top down.

12
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:47,044
Five of Spades, Queen of Diamonds,
Jack of Spades, Ace of Hearts,

13
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:51,889
Seven of Diamonds, plus the Six of Clubs,
King of Clubs, and Two of Diamonds.

14
00:00:54,560 --> 00:00:55,736
He guessed them all!

15
00:00:55,940 --> 00:00:58,352
And that's after Darby shuffled the deck!

16
00:00:58,460 --> 00:00:59,680
How did you do that?

17
00:00:59,940 --> 00:01:02,881
I could rattle off the
entire deck if I wanted to.

18
00:01:03,540 --> 00:01:05,481
Remember my request from earlier?

19
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:07,237
While you were shuffling the cards,

20
00:01:07,320 --> 00:01:10,732
Star Platinum was busy memorizing
their order in the deck.

21
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,824
Quite the interesting strategy.

22
00:01:13,360 --> 00:01:14,190
That said,

23
00:01:14,273 --> 00:01:16,737
defeating your plan is a
simple matter of shuffling the

24
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:19,517
cards in a manner that
obstructs your vision of them.

25
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:20,860
Are you that dense?

26
00:01:21,240 --> 00:01:25,477
Cheating is going to be damn near impossible
as long as you have me as an opponent.

27
00:01:25,560 --> 00:01:28,384
Just something I thought
you should be aware of.

28
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:29,970
Okay.

29
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:43,860
The security seal.

30
00:01:44,080 --> 00:01:46,877
An unbroken seal is an
irrefutable confirmation

31
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:50,019
that the deck has not been
tampered with in any way.

32
00:02:01,160 --> 00:02:03,260
Well, there's only one Joker here.

33
00:02:03,460 --> 00:02:04,677
Don't see anything unusual.

34
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:06,180
It's a normal deck.

35
00:02:10,980 --> 00:02:13,980
The page number is 538. 540?

36
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:16,260
No, page 556.

37
00:02:18,180 --> 00:02:19,780
I still got it.

38
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:24,320
My ability to discern page numbers
by touch is as sharp as ever.

39
00:02:24,820 --> 00:02:29,120
It's true that Jotaro's Star Platinum
has incredible visual prowess,

40
00:02:29,260 --> 00:02:33,737
but I can remember the placement of
anything simply through the use of touch.

41
00:02:33,820 --> 00:02:35,197
Shuffle them all you want.

42
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:38,340
I still know the exact
location of every card.

43
00:02:46,160 --> 00:02:47,820
Okay, open the game.

44
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:52,740
Looks like it's the Ten of Hearts.

45
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,680
I drew the Seven of Clubs.

46
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:56,999
Then it seems like I'll be dealing.

47
00:02:57,940 --> 00:03:01,820
Alright, I need to shuffle
so Star Platinum can't see.

48
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:10,020
If you would cut the deck.

49
00:03:23,620 --> 00:03:25,326
Thank you, and now I'll deal.

50
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:28,860
One for Jotaro, one for me.

51
00:03:29,160 --> 00:03:31,560
One for Jotaro, one for me.

52
00:03:38,340 --> 00:03:40,900
I don't understand. What happened?

53
00:03:41,940 --> 00:03:43,420
Jotaro! His finger!

54
00:03:43,660 --> 00:03:47,277
Why the devil would you use Star
Platinum to break Darby's finger?

55
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:51,820
Like I said, you're not going to cheat
when you're playing against me. Huh?

56
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:53,060
He tried to cheat?

57
00:03:53,260 --> 00:03:55,697
But he was only dealing
the cards, wasn't he?

58
00:03:55,780 --> 00:03:58,309
I didn't notice him do
anything suspicious.

59
00:03:58,520 --> 00:04:00,177
That's what he wanted us to think.

60
00:04:00,260 --> 00:04:03,260
but take a good look at
the cards in his left hand.

61
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:04,980
I see now!

62
00:04:05,240 --> 00:04:07,122
The second card is sticking out!

63
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:10,037
That's the card he tried to deal me.

64
00:04:10,120 --> 00:04:13,217
The entire time he was
pretending to deal the top card,

65
00:04:13,300 --> 00:04:17,065
but the truth is he was dealing
me the second card from the top.

66
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:21,142
That being the case, it means the
top card would have gone to him.

67
00:04:21,780 --> 00:04:23,577
If he'd gotten his hands on it,

68
00:04:23,660 --> 00:04:26,617
the cheating bastard would
have had a total of three tens.

69
00:04:26,700 --> 00:04:29,340
This maneuver is known as the second deal.

70
00:04:30,260 --> 00:04:33,737
A devious sleight-of-hand technique
involving the dealer throwing out the

71
00:04:33,820 --> 00:04:38,291
second card in the deck instead of
dealing the top card as one would expect.

72
00:04:38,920 --> 00:04:41,737
When the technique is
executed by a professional,

73
00:04:41,820 --> 00:04:44,761
the cheat is almost
undetectable to the naked eye.

74
00:04:45,180 --> 00:04:46,709
And if that wasn't enough,

75
00:04:47,060 --> 00:04:50,797
Darby can discern the location of
every card in the deck by touch.

76
00:04:50,880 --> 00:04:52,980
You brutish imbecile!

77
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:55,100
How dare you break my finger!

78
00:04:57,080 --> 00:04:59,198
I was playing nice with that attack.

79
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:02,499
You should count yourself
lucky I didn't rip it off.

80
00:05:03,240 --> 00:05:04,280
Good grief.

81
00:05:04,640 --> 00:05:07,287
I guess I can't let you
cut the deck anymore.

82
00:05:08,260 --> 00:05:10,789
Someone else is going
to do it from now on.

83
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:13,652
That boy on the hill looks up to the job.

84
00:05:15,420 --> 00:05:16,840
Have it your way.

85
00:05:17,340 --> 00:05:20,020
Hey, Avdol, ask him over right away.

86
00:05:20,940 --> 00:05:22,100
Most impressive.

87
00:05:23,240 --> 00:05:25,977
Successful cheating requires
the element of surprise,

88
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:29,340
and it takes more than
sharp eyes to prevent that.

89
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:33,462
It appears I underestimated you
as you saw through my second deal.

90
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:36,900
I'll accept my fractured
finger as proper punishment,

91
00:05:37,220 --> 00:05:41,620
but from here on I'll devote my full
concentration to winning the game.

92
00:05:42,520 --> 00:05:43,350
Jotaro.

93
00:05:44,040 --> 00:05:48,577
I've not done so since my
colossal gamble on May 17th, 1986.

94
00:05:48,660 --> 00:05:53,677
I was playing against a Japanese
man known as Chase Mayama as the

95
00:05:53,760 --> 00:05:57,637
victor my spoils included his eight
Tokyo properties and his soul.

96
00:05:57,720 --> 00:06:02,300
I will say this for Mayama wealth
didn't dull his gambler's instincts.

97
00:06:05,080 --> 00:06:08,557
It's only fair that I warn you I'm
not here on behalf of Lord Dio.

98
00:06:08,640 --> 00:06:12,052
I am here due to the simple
fact that I am a born gambler.

99
00:06:13,500 --> 00:06:15,977
What do you think you're
doing those souls are mr.

100
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:17,413
Joe stars and Bulgarefs

101
00:06:27,900 --> 00:06:31,677
I've done nothing more than split
their souls into six chips each.

102
00:06:31,760 --> 00:06:33,936
I'm sure you know this, but in poker,

103
00:06:34,020 --> 00:06:38,020
if you're on the verge of losing,
it's perfectly acceptable to fold.

104
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:39,310
However,

105
00:06:39,393 --> 00:06:41,477
if you use up all the chips for the ante,

106
00:06:41,560 --> 00:06:43,957
there's no way to bet and
the game doesn't work.

107
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,440
To put it plainly,

108
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:50,197
winning back six chips is the equivalent
of winning the soul of one of your friends.

109
00:06:50,280 --> 00:06:51,110
Makes sense?

110
00:06:52,040 --> 00:06:53,700
All right then, Jotaro.

111
00:06:53,980 --> 00:06:58,037
If you still want to play, you'll have
the opportunity to win back the chips.

112
00:06:58,120 --> 00:07:01,100
But before that, I need
to hear you say the words.

113
00:07:04,340 --> 00:07:05,320
With pleasure.

114
00:07:05,640 --> 00:07:07,934
I'll bet my soul on the game's outcome.

115
00:07:08,220 --> 00:07:09,050
Okay.

116
00:07:09,700 --> 00:07:10,530
Jotaro!

117
00:07:13,020 --> 00:07:17,726
The pure white chips in front of you are
a physical representation of your soul.

118
00:07:18,260 --> 00:07:23,760
Once I procured all six of those chips,
your soul will be added to my collection.

119
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:47,760
For my opening action, I shall
bet one chip of Polnareff's soul.

120
00:07:50,200 --> 00:07:51,160
Let's begin.

121
00:07:51,720 --> 00:07:56,480
When beginning a new game of poker, each
player is dealt a total of five cards.

122
00:07:56,760 --> 00:07:59,878
Players can improve their
hand by swapping out cards.

123
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,977
Though it seems
straightforward on the surface,

124
00:08:05,060 --> 00:08:09,766
it's the betting aspect that makes poker
a game of determination and psychology.

125
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:12,780
Now then, what to do?

126
00:08:13,060 --> 00:08:14,413
Ah, I think I'll raise.

127
00:08:17,180 --> 00:08:21,960
Jotaro, you should bear in mind that
those six chips beside you are your soul.

128
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:25,400
Make sure you think carefully
before making a move.

129
00:08:26,500 --> 00:08:29,897
Listen, it's okay if you don't
understand what's going on.

130
00:08:29,980 --> 00:08:31,157
Don't worry yourself.

131
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:35,475
You just focus your attention on
cutting and dealing the cards, alright?

132
00:08:36,060 --> 00:08:37,660
Give me three cards.

133
00:08:45,220 --> 00:08:46,580
Would you look at that?

134
00:08:46,780 --> 00:08:48,240
Such a serious glare.

135
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:51,260
Behind it must be an outstanding hand.

136
00:08:51,640 --> 00:08:55,460
I suppose I'll play it safe for
now and bet one more Polnareff.

137
00:08:55,680 --> 00:08:56,720
Call one.

138
00:08:57,080 --> 00:09:01,198
If you don't fold, you'll need three
chips per game at the very least.

139
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:04,340
All right, bring it on, Jotaro.

140
00:09:07,140 --> 00:09:09,180
Two pair with eights and nines.

141
00:09:10,660 --> 00:09:11,920
Hmm, that's too bad.

142
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:14,440
Two pair, jacks and queens.

143
00:09:16,240 --> 00:09:17,540
Oh, no!

144
00:09:17,800 --> 00:09:19,360
My, that was a close one.

145
00:09:19,580 --> 00:09:21,933
I was on the verge of a crushing defeat.

146
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,780
But as it stands...

147
00:09:35,260 --> 00:09:37,357
He only has three left.

148
00:09:37,440 --> 00:09:39,520
Jotaro, what are you...

149
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:42,880
Okay, next game. Deal the cards.

150
00:09:51,140 --> 00:09:53,640
You should be careful what you wish for.

151
00:09:53,860 --> 00:09:56,100
The next game may well be your last.

152
00:10:01,720 --> 00:10:03,460
I'll change one card.

153
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,460
What's the problem, Jotaro?

154
00:10:18,880 --> 00:10:21,017
Hurry up and check your
hands so you can make

155
00:10:21,100 --> 00:10:23,757
a decision as to whether
you'll change or fold.

156
00:10:23,840 --> 00:10:24,940
Hey, Jotaro?

157
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,300
No, it's fine.

158
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:30,820
These cards will do.

159
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:35,100
So sorry. Come again?

160
00:10:35,400 --> 00:10:36,817
There must be some confusion.

161
00:10:36,900 --> 00:10:38,640
Perhaps I misheard you.

162
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:41,657
I could have sworn I heard
you say these cards will do.

163
00:10:41,740 --> 00:10:42,916
No, you heard right.

164
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,529
I'm fine with these cards.

165
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:46,739
I'll play the round with this hand.

166
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:48,390
Obviously!

167
00:10:48,473 --> 00:10:49,797
What I'm trying to ask is,

168
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:53,998
do you intend to play those cards
without so much as glancing at them?

169
00:10:54,340 --> 00:10:55,516
These cards will do.

170
00:10:57,220 --> 00:10:59,060
Enough subterfuge! Answer me!

171
00:10:59,160 --> 00:11:01,237
How can you play a round
with any sort of confidence

172
00:11:01,320 --> 00:11:03,537
if you don't even look at
the cards in your hand?

173
00:11:03,620 --> 00:11:04,450
Need a favor.

174
00:11:04,880 --> 00:11:05,710
You in?

175
00:11:06,460 --> 00:11:07,290
Favor?

176
00:11:07,373 --> 00:11:09,595
Of course, but answer something first.

177
00:11:09,840 --> 00:11:12,257
Why are you hell-bent on
not looking at your cards?

178
00:11:12,340 --> 00:11:13,281
Damn it, Jotaro!

179
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:15,087
I demand that you answer me!

180
00:11:15,220 --> 00:11:16,060
Let's see now.

181
00:11:16,320 --> 00:11:17,614
Raise you another two.

182
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:23,988
While I'm at it, I'll
throw in Avdol's soul.

183
00:11:25,820 --> 00:11:26,650
What?

184
00:11:29,520 --> 00:11:32,620
I admit, you're an
impressive opponent, Darby.

185
00:11:32,960 --> 00:11:35,357
Sure, you're no match for
our stands physically.

186
00:11:35,440 --> 00:11:38,793
But under pressure, you can
be amazingly calm and clever.

187
00:11:38,960 --> 00:11:42,017
Suffice it to say, I'm not much
in terms of being a gambler.

188
00:11:42,100 --> 00:11:44,688
It'd be easy for you
to read me like a book.

189
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:47,372
So I could never defeat someone like you.

190
00:11:47,460 --> 00:11:49,989
But I have the utmost
confidence in Jotaro.

191
00:11:50,380 --> 00:11:54,637
I don't know why he won't look at his
cards, but that's none of my concern.

192
00:11:54,720 --> 00:11:58,637
If he asks for my soul, I won't
hesitate to put my life on the line.

193
00:11:58,720 --> 00:12:01,485
My soul is in Jotaro's
more than capable hands.

194
00:12:02,440 --> 00:12:04,381
So that's how we're playing this.

195
00:12:07,280 --> 00:12:09,597
It's become apparent
that the two of you have

196
00:12:09,680 --> 00:12:12,317
succumbed to the pressure
of our little game.

197
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:15,120
You there, I believe
you owe me another card.

198
00:12:15,320 --> 00:12:17,560
Hurry and deal me. Yes, sir.

199
00:12:25,600 --> 00:12:28,500
I dealt just as you asked, Master Darby.

200
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:32,240
His hand is worthless,
there's no doubt about it.

201
00:12:32,440 --> 00:12:34,940
My skills as a dealer never fail.

202
00:12:35,720 --> 00:12:36,620
You've won.

203
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:38,100
I know you have.

204
00:12:39,340 --> 00:12:42,577
Jotaro's under the assumption the
boy has nothing to do with this.

205
00:12:42,660 --> 00:12:45,077
But little does he know
everyone in this cafe

206
00:12:45,160 --> 00:12:47,748
and within sight of
this place works for me.

207
00:12:48,640 --> 00:12:50,880
Even the bartender and those men.

208
00:12:51,220 --> 00:12:57,100
No matter what, I can't fail, as my directive
is to make sure Jotaro's hand is weak.

209
00:12:57,440 --> 00:13:00,520
Still, not looking at the
cards was a bold move.

210
00:13:00,700 --> 00:13:03,380
He cut me by surprise, albeit briefly.

211
00:13:04,020 --> 00:13:05,780
It's clearly a bluff.

212
00:13:06,180 --> 00:13:08,020
How dare he bluff against me?

213
00:13:08,420 --> 00:13:11,480
Does the fool really think
I'll lie down and fold?

214
00:13:11,960 --> 00:13:13,320
Huh, very well.

215
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:18,200
If that's your game, I'll
match you with six Polnare.

216
00:13:18,720 --> 00:13:21,380
And I raise you Joseph's soul.

217
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:23,980
What do you think?

218
00:13:24,160 --> 00:13:25,460
Fifteen chips total.

219
00:13:26,720 --> 00:13:27,550
What?

220
00:13:27,633 --> 00:13:28,463
Hold on a minute.

221
00:13:28,546 --> 00:13:29,397
That's not fair.

222
00:13:29,480 --> 00:13:32,497
How can you raise your auntie when
Jotaro doesn't have any more chips?

223
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:34,380
He's out of chips, you say?

224
00:13:34,640 --> 00:13:36,522
There's an easy way to fix that.

225
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:37,700
What do you mean?

226
00:13:38,040 --> 00:13:40,117
Rectifying your chip conundrum is simple,

227
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:42,729
as long as my stand
has a written contract.

228
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:46,477
Once the deal is done, it'll
have Card blanche to take a soul.

229
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:49,207
And exactly whose soul
are you talking about?

230
00:13:50,120 --> 00:13:51,537
Kakuane's in the hospital.

231
00:13:51,620 --> 00:13:53,780
Why don't you simply bed his soul?

232
00:13:54,720 --> 00:13:55,550
What?!

233
00:13:55,633 --> 00:13:56,580
Panic, fool.

234
00:13:57,060 --> 00:13:58,800
Show me your doubt and fear.

235
00:13:59,120 --> 00:14:01,780
Let me see you lose that cool composure.

236
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:04,240
How dare he try to bluff me.

237
00:14:04,620 --> 00:14:06,267
After I'm finished with him,

238
00:14:06,440 --> 00:14:10,200
that poker face will be a contorted
ball of anguish and misery.

239
00:14:10,720 --> 00:14:11,920
Sounds like a plan.

240
00:14:13,180 --> 00:14:15,415
I'll see your bed with Kakyoin's soul.

241
00:14:17,960 --> 00:14:19,820
Wait, Jotaro, you can't!

242
00:14:19,960 --> 00:14:22,937
Bedding a man's soul without
his knowledge is so uncouth!

243
00:14:23,020 --> 00:14:24,667
Well, it is kind of selfish.

244
00:14:28,240 --> 00:14:30,757
Hey, Jotaro, what did you just do?

245
00:14:30,840 --> 00:14:32,480
What did I just do?

246
00:14:32,700 --> 00:14:34,117
What do you mean by that?

247
00:14:34,200 --> 00:14:35,376
You lit a cigarette!

248
00:14:38,300 --> 00:14:39,594
What's wrong with you?

249
00:14:39,720 --> 00:14:41,485
Not feeling well or something?

250
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:46,810
Impertinent!

251
00:14:46,893 --> 00:14:48,580
Why is he so confident?

252
00:14:49,120 --> 00:14:50,097
Could he have...

253
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:54,300
Could he have used Star Platinum to
swap the cards without my knowing?

254
00:15:12,920 --> 00:15:14,979
Stupid brat, what are you thinking?

255
00:15:15,160 --> 00:15:17,277
Don't look at me with
that worried grimace.

256
00:15:17,360 --> 00:15:21,300
If Jotaro finds out you work
for me, I'll murder you.

257
00:15:26,820 --> 00:15:29,557
Compose yourself, I have four kings.

258
00:15:29,640 --> 00:15:32,720
The only hands that could
beat me are four aces,

259
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:36,280
a straight flush, or a
joker-led five-of-a-kind.

260
00:15:37,420 --> 00:15:40,244
In order to get his mitts
on any of those hands,

261
00:15:40,560 --> 00:15:43,089
Jotaro would have to
switch all five cards.

262
00:15:43,200 --> 00:15:44,540
A challenge indeed.

263
00:15:45,080 --> 00:15:49,157
With Star Platinum's speed, there's a
chance he could have switched a card.

264
00:15:49,240 --> 00:15:50,070
But five?

265
00:15:50,200 --> 00:15:54,040
Could he really do that right
under my nose? Impossible!

266
00:15:55,540 --> 00:15:58,717
There's no way I could have
missed him replacing all five.

267
00:15:58,800 --> 00:16:04,340
I'm the great Darby, the king of
games, master at the art of gambling.

268
00:16:05,020 --> 00:16:06,902
I've had enough of this, Jotaro.

269
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,660
Your time has come.

270
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:13,580
He lit that cigarette to psych me
out, so now I know he's bluffing.

271
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:20,420
You're kidding me!

272
00:16:20,560 --> 00:16:21,736
You got a drink too?

273
00:16:21,860 --> 00:16:24,480
When did you have a
chance to, you bastard?

274
00:16:24,620 --> 00:16:26,217
How dare you make fun of me?

275
00:16:26,300 --> 00:16:27,497
Let's finish this.

276
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:29,680
My hand is unbeatable. Hold it.

277
00:16:30,800 --> 00:16:34,447
Why are you jumping the gun when
I haven't raised the pot yet?

278
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:39,580
Raise the pot?

279
00:16:39,760 --> 00:16:42,407
No, you don't have
anything to raise it with.

280
00:16:45,900 --> 00:16:47,257
That's where you're wrong.

281
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:50,040
I'll raise you with my
mother's soul. What?

282
00:16:51,140 --> 00:16:52,640
Are you out of your mind?

283
00:16:52,960 --> 00:16:55,607
Jojuro, why would you
bet your mother's soul?

284
00:16:59,900 --> 00:17:03,717
The entire reason I came to Egypt in
the first place was to save my mother.

285
00:17:03,800 --> 00:17:06,417
So if I end up losing
here, she'll die anyway.

286
00:17:06,500 --> 00:17:08,441
She won't mind if I bet her soul.

287
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:09,780
So then, Darby,

288
00:17:09,980 --> 00:17:14,417
for your sake, I hope you have something
to bet that matches my mother's soul.

289
00:17:14,500 --> 00:17:15,330
I know.

290
00:17:16,420 --> 00:17:20,380
For your auntie, I want you to
tell me the secret of Dio Stand.

291
00:17:25,680 --> 00:17:27,209
Judging from his reaction,

292
00:17:27,900 --> 00:17:30,020
He indeed knows Dio's secret.

293
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:34,017
Unfortunately for him, Dio
doesn't take treason sitting down.

294
00:17:34,100 --> 00:17:38,159
If he tells us the information we
want to know, he's as good as dead.

295
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:41,470
Jotaro,

296
00:17:41,553 --> 00:17:44,057
if you're confident enough
to bet your mother's soul,

297
00:17:44,140 --> 00:17:46,517
you're sure your hand
will win, aren't you?

298
00:17:46,600 --> 00:17:48,718
You wouldn't let us down, would you?

299
00:17:49,020 --> 00:17:51,079
You've got the winning hand, right?

300
00:17:51,420 --> 00:17:52,250
Jotaro?

301
00:17:58,920 --> 00:18:01,744
Come on, are you going
to call my bluff or fold?

302
00:18:01,960 --> 00:18:05,080
Decision time, spit it out already. Jar B!

303
00:18:15,880 --> 00:18:16,960
I'll say it.

304
00:18:23,580 --> 00:18:25,680
I'll say it, Darmot!

305
00:18:31,360 --> 00:18:32,800
I'll say it!

306
00:18:32,960 --> 00:18:34,897
I'm the world's greatest gambler!

307
00:18:34,980 --> 00:18:36,140
I can do this!

308
00:18:36,360 --> 00:18:37,600
I'll call!

309
00:18:46,760 --> 00:18:48,600
I'm going to call!

310
00:18:50,660 --> 00:18:51,490
Call!

311
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:19,180
I can't do it.

312
00:19:19,340 --> 00:19:20,257
I'm petrified.

313
00:19:20,340 --> 00:19:23,120
I'm too terrified to say the words!

314
00:19:26,860 --> 00:19:27,957
I can't...

315
00:19:28,040 --> 00:19:29,560
I can't breathe!

316
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,600
That's unbelievable!

317
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:44,551
His eyes rolled into the back of his head!

318
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:48,197
How is it possible for someone to
faint while they're on their feet?

319
00:19:48,280 --> 00:19:49,980
He's completely lost it.

320
00:19:50,160 --> 00:19:51,631
The pressure was too much

321
00:19:57,740 --> 00:19:58,570
Mr.

322
00:19:58,653 --> 00:20:00,977
Joestar and Polnareff's souls
are returning to their bodies.

323
00:20:01,060 --> 00:20:01,890
Thank heavens

324
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:07,633
Mentally he's already forfeited the game

325
00:20:08,080 --> 00:20:10,040
Deep down he knew he had lost.

326
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:12,420
That's why the souls were released

327
00:20:13,460 --> 00:20:14,580
Four kings!

328
00:20:14,920 --> 00:20:17,685
Are you telling me he
had four kings all along?

329
00:20:18,280 --> 00:20:23,104
Jotaro, I have to know what cards you had
in your hand to inspire such confidence.

330
00:20:26,700 --> 00:20:27,680
Like I thought.

331
00:20:29,700 --> 00:20:32,420
Your hand was shit, absolute shit!

332
00:20:33,120 --> 00:20:35,557
Even with Star Platinum's
incredible speed,

333
00:20:35,640 --> 00:20:37,057
he wouldn't have been able to swap cards?

334
00:20:37,140 --> 00:20:39,097
in front of an expert gambler like Darby.

335
00:20:39,180 --> 00:20:41,137
It's a good thing my
bluff and intimidation

336
00:20:41,220 --> 00:20:44,080
worked so well with such a worthless hand.

337
00:20:44,380 --> 00:20:47,337
Good grief, had I known it was
this crappy, I would have freaked.

338
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:48,250
What?

339
00:20:48,333 --> 00:20:49,617
What do you mean you'd have freaked?

340
00:20:49,700 --> 00:20:53,700
Jotaro, don't tell me that you bet
our souls on that worthless hand.

341
00:21:10,060 --> 00:21:13,957
It would appear as though his
collection of souls has been released.

342
00:21:14,040 --> 00:21:15,497
Come on, everyone!

343
00:21:15,580 --> 00:21:17,580
Let's play a game of Mahjong!

344
00:21:18,100 --> 00:21:19,982
Backgammon is a lot of fun, too!

345
00:21:20,140 --> 00:21:23,820
Or we can play a game of dice,
even though I don't have any!

346
00:21:24,320 --> 00:21:26,780
Darby of the Osiris Stand! Retired!

347
00:21:28,300 --> 00:21:32,437
I doubt that we'll be able to pry
Dio's secret out of him in this state.

348
00:21:32,520 --> 00:21:33,350
That's true.

349
00:21:33,433 --> 00:21:35,046
He was a formidable opponent.

350
00:21:35,300 --> 00:21:38,817
It's humbling to admit this, but he
almost took us all out single-handedly.

351
00:21:38,900 --> 00:21:41,077
The guy was a force to be reckoned with.

352
00:21:41,160 --> 00:21:43,160
Indeed, he was a fierce adversary.

353
00:21:43,620 --> 00:21:45,679
Ugh, I feel like death warmed over.

354
00:21:46,700 --> 00:21:49,876
Well, I guess we can't be
the heroes in every episode.

355
00:22:16,180 --> 00:22:17,620
Thank you.

356
00:22:51,200 --> 00:22:53,340
Thank you.
